# Derived by hand from Semantics Appendix B, `Split`: the pieces between the matches the iteration rule finds, so `k` matches give `k + 1` texts and empty ones are kept ("a,,b" is three, "" is one empty text, a separator at either end gives an empty text there); the empty pattern matches at every character boundary, so it cuts "abc" into its characters with an empty text at each end, and "" into two empty texts.
